WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:01.669
(upbeat techno music)

00:00:01.669 --> 00:00:03.069
- [Keith] Anything that you do

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.328
definitely has the element of power.

00:00:05.328 --> 00:00:06.440
When you're actually out there,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.739
and you're actually voguing
or you’re actually walking,

00:00:08.739 --> 00:00:09.859
and the beat is taking you,

00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:11.859
then you just go for it.

00:00:12.728 --> 00:00:15.311
(upbeat music)

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.528
- My name is Keith Holt.

00:00:19.528 --> 00:00:22.928
When I'm out at the balls,
I become Keith Ebony

00:00:22.928 --> 00:00:24.727
the crown prince of Baltimore.

00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:27.628
Voguing, it's an underground art form,

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:31.078
that was brought to like throw
shade on the dance floor.

00:00:31.078 --> 00:00:34.469
Ballroom in general was
developed to be underground.

00:00:34.469 --> 00:00:38.560
Partially because of so
much stigma and hate

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.698
that the LGBT community have experienced.

00:00:41.698 --> 00:00:45.865
This is a place that you can
be anything that you want to be

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.299
James is like that new
generation of voguers.

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:52.829
- How you doin? I'm the
Legendary Lil James Khan.

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:54.789
I'm the vogue fem extraordinaire.

00:00:54.789 --> 00:00:58.109
- [Keith] He is like the
Beyoncé of the ballroom scene.

00:00:58.109 --> 00:00:59.691
Mook is my best friend.

00:00:59.691 --> 00:01:02.650
- I am the voice of
Baltimore, Mook Mizrahi.

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:04.067
The dramatic one.

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:07.339
- [Keith] He commentates, he vogue.

00:01:07.339 --> 00:01:10.457
James, Mook, and myself
are some people that

00:01:10.457 --> 00:01:13.320
are really leading the next generation.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:15.120
(upbeat music)

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.760
- [Keith] I work for the
Baltimore city health department.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.378
I'm the youth outreach coordinator.

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.259
With that I kind of come up
with the different events.

00:01:21.259 --> 00:01:22.909
And something that kept coming up was,

00:01:22.909 --> 00:01:24.091
why not throw a ball?

00:01:24.091 --> 00:01:25.411
So we have our free ball.

00:01:25.411 --> 00:01:27.971
And because Baltimore
has a high rate in HIV,

00:01:27.971 --> 00:01:30.699
that's why we make sure that
every event that we have

00:01:30.699 --> 00:01:34.309
we do offer both HIV
testing and HIV linkage

00:01:34.309 --> 00:01:36.280
to treatment as well.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.000
For me it's really like
this is not just a job.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.099
This is my community.

00:01:42.099 --> 00:01:43.651
These are people that I know.

00:01:43.651 --> 00:01:47.189
Ballroom is not just a
extracurricular activity anymore.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:49.098
It's actually now a part of my life.

00:01:49.098 --> 00:01:51.681
(upbeat music)

